 "path": "continual_arc_task79_rule.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC observation: binary color-frequency relabeling\n\nIn task-79f4fb55, the grid had two colors, 5 and 8. The correct transformation was: count both colors; recolor the more frequent (majority) color to 0, and recolor the less frequent (minority) color to the original majority color. Here 8 occurred more often than 5, so 8→0 and 5→8. This matched the demos: demo 1 had 5/7 with 5 dominant (5→7, 7→0); demo 2 had 5/6 with 5 dominant (5→6, 6→0). Thus infer the mapping from frequency rather than fixed color IDs. Verify only for matching two-color binary-grid task instances."
